# Shared-radio profiles for UCanDrop's OWL backend.
#
# A profile is a narrow driver workaround, not proof that the hardware can
# inject, receive, or complete a transfer.  Every entry remains gated by the
# runtime association, regulatory, monitor-capability, and OWL readiness checks;
# `untested` also requires allow-untested=1 in /etc/ucandrop.
#
#   status     tested: this driver's strategy is reviewed for the release;
#              runtime association/regulatory/monitor gates still apply
#              and this does not claim every board or kernel works
#              untested: no portable completion proof is claimed; explicit
#              allow-untested=1 is required
#   mode       shared: AWDL shares the currently associated AP channel
#   mon_mac    station: monitor carries the station MAC; own: use a local
#              monitor MAC and pass the station MAC to OWL with -m when needed
#   reconnect  yes: reconnect the same managed device after monitor teardown
#   mt76_pm    yes: guard mt76 runtime power management for the session
#
# driver   status    mode    mon_mac  reconnect  mt76_pm  notes
mt7925e    tested    shared  station  yes        yes       Generic MT76 monitor/association workaround for the reviewed mt7925e driver strategy; runtime gates still apply.
*          untested  shared  station  no         no        Generic shared-radio attempt; requires monitor injection and a supported associated AWDL channel.
